{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1030158-conquering-heroes","id":1030158,"title":"Conquering Heroes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-11T11:37:17-08:00","id":1030158,"title":"Conquering Heroes","content":"Do you think you can break the Hero's narrative? Are you sure? <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/202615/Night-Horrors-Conquering-Heroes?affiliate_id=498510\" target=\"_blank\">The Conquering Heroes are here to put you to the test. </a><br /> <br /> Discuss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T12:21:03-08:00","id":1030173,"title":"","content":"The Insatiable are cool. I don't understand some of their mechanics though.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Storyteller then makes an extended and contested roll using the Insatiable\u2019s Strength + Satiety versus the Beast\u2019s Composure + Willpower. For each point of Satiety above 5 the Beast has, her player receives a -1 penalty to her roll, and for each point below 5, he receives a +1 bonus. <b>For each success the Insatiable achieves, they move the Beast\u2019s Composure or Presence down by 1</b>. When both Attributes reach zero, the Insatiable successfully subverts the Beast\u2019s consciousness and gains control for one hour for each point of Satiety the Beast has. </div> </div> </div>Is that every success rolled? Or every successful roll? <br /> <br /> What happens if the Beast wins the roll?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T12:36:19-08:00","id":1030185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1030158-conquering-heroes?p=1030173#post1030173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Insatiable are cool. I don't understand some of their mechanics though.<br /> <br /> <br /> Is that every success rolled? Or every successful roll?<br /> <br /> What happens if the Beast wins the roll?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably something to save for the errata thread when it goes up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T12:49:47-08:00","id":1030195,"title":"","content":"This is exciting. I can't wait to buy it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T13:02:14-08:00","id":1030202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1030158-conquering-heroes?p=1030173#post1030173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is that every success rolled? Or every successful roll?</div> </div> </div> </div>Since it says every success, I'd imagine it's referring to every 8, 9, or 10 rolled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T13:08:46-08:00","id":1030207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1030158-conquering-heroes?p=1030202#post1030202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Since it says every success, I'd imagine it's referring to every 8, 9, or 10 rolled.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Inodiv means that, because it's an Extended Contested roll, it's a little unclear what the Beast's resistance does if it's every success.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T13:11:26-08:00","id":1030209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1030158-conquering-heroes?p=1030207#post1030207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Inodiv means that, because it's an Extended Contested roll, it's a little unclear what the Beast's resistance does if it's every success.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I see. Well, contested actions pit two groups of successes against one another, successes basically cancelling each other out until one side has more. So in this case it would be every 8, 9 and 10 more than the Beast.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T13:16:08-08:00","id":1030211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1030158-conquering-heroes?p=1030209#post1030209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh I see. Well, contested actions pit two groups of successes against one another, successes basically cancelling each other out until one side has more. So in this case it would be every 8, 9 and 10 more than the Beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't usually work that way, though? At least I don't think it does by default... Whatever the case, if that's the intent, I agree that it could use a clarification.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T13:20:50-08:00","id":1030213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1030158-conquering-heroes?p=1030211#post1030211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It doesn't usually work that way, though? At least I don't think it does by default... Whatever the case, if that's the intent, I agree that it could use a clarification.</div> </div> </div> </div>This would be the first instance I'm aware of in the entire system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T13:25:29-08:00","id":1030217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1030158-conquering-heroes?p=1030213#post1030213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This would be the first instance I'm aware of in the entire system.</div> </div> </div> </div>'When two characters are competing, and you only need to know who comes out on top, use a contested action. In a contested action, each player rolls a pool for their character (such as an Attribute + Skill pool), and the character for whom the most successes are rolled wins the contest.'<br /> <br /> It doesn't actually cancel out the Successes, but the effect is similar. If I roll 1 success and you roll 2, only your extra one counts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T13:29:37-08:00","id":1030219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1030158-conquering-heroes?p=1030217#post1030217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 'When two characters are competing, and you only need to know who comes out on top, use a contested action. In a contested action, each player rolls a pool for their character (such as an Attribute + Skill pool), and the character for whom the most successes are rolled wins the contest.'<br /> <br /> It doesn't actually cancel out the Successes, but the effect is similar. If I roll 1 success and you roll 2, only your extra one counts.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's partially that contested actions aren't typically extended, so they don't often have set successes. Anyway, it's not that hard to clarify, so hopefully the errata thread will be up soonish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T13:30:38-08:00","id":1030221,"title":"","content":"So can someone tell me just what the Insatiable are?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T13:31:42-08:00","id":1030223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1030158-conquering-heroes?p=1030217#post1030217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't actually cancel out the Successes, but the effect is similar. If I roll 1 success and you roll 2, only your extra one counts.</div> </div> </div> </div>The text doesn't support that at all. Contested Rolls Track Pass/Fail, there's no subtracting successes based on the other party's roll. The system has never worked that way, which makes the bit of text in this book a really weird implementation that is almost definitely some sort of error.<br /> <br /> One reason the two concepts really aren't that similar: If I roll 5 and you roll 4, I still get an exceptional success, not a single, simple success.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T13:33:28-08:00","id":1030224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1030158-conquering-heroes?p=1030221#post1030221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So can someone tell me just what the Insatiable are?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. Here you go!<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Lamashtu. The Obscene Ones. The Nightmares of Beasts. No matter their true name, the Beasts<br /> know them by one name in particular that best describes who and what they are: the Insatiable. They are not<br /> just creatures whose Hunger cannot be sated, but entities that forcefully intrude into the world and disrupt<br /> the ebb and flow of the Primordial Dream with their actions. They are creatures made of<br /> concepts alien to how humanity thinks. They are the nightmare that is the Hunger left<br /> unchecked and given horrific form, and they feed not just upon the dreams of man<br /> but on the fears of the Beasts themselves. They are monsters whose hunger cannot<br /> be reined in, and it is from this lust to fill the emptiness inside of them<br /> that they gain their powers. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T13:35:11-08:00","id":1030225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1030158-conquering-heroes?p=1030223#post1030223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The text doesn't support that at all. Contested Rolls Track Pass/Fail, there's no subtracting successes based on the other party's roll. The system has never worked that way, which makes the bit of text in this book a really weird implementation that is almost definitely some sort of error.<br /> <br /> One reason the two concepts really aren't that similar: If I roll 5 and you roll 4, I still get an exceptional success, not a single, simple success.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why I said similar, and not exactly the same. I probably could have used a different term, but there's very few situations where it would matter. Exceptional Successes are a special case, and don't matter in the example you're asking about, where there's no Exceptional Success bonus and all that matters is whether you've gotten more successes than the other person, and possibly how many.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T14:02:04-08:00","id":1030235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1030158-conquering-heroes?p=1030223#post1030223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One reason the two concepts really aren't that similar: If I roll 5 and you roll 4, I still get an exceptional success, not a single, simple success.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, does not you get in Contested Rolls the Exceptional Success only if you got 5 or <b>more</b> over your opponent. I.e. if my oponent roll 2 success, I need 7 success myself to get Exceptional Success?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T14:04:22-08:00","id":1030238,"title":"","content":"Well, I may have a strained relationship with Beast, but I bought the book.<br /> <br /> Heroes are officially redeemed as a concept to me. I think the writers realized that on some level being unable to get the Primordial Dream to <i>shut up </i>is a tragic condition, and apart from the explicit &quot;terrible people&quot;, the examples all come off as sympathetic, and often epic, antagonists. I like Martin West and the Soul-Taker best so far (the first because he's the same weird combination of inhuman and pitiable that Beasts are, the second because she's a pretty unique twist on the mastermind).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T14:08:34-08:00","id":1030241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1030158-conquering-heroes?p=1030238#post1030238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heroes are officially redeemed as a concept to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not making them all out to be horrible people has helped. But while the book offers a lot of interesting antagonists, Beast still doesn't seem appealing from a gaming point of view, for me, at least. I think it would be really big with the 'I don't like these covenants or tribes or orders and so forth' crowd. A more pared down 'play a monster' game.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T14:10:48-08:00","id":1030243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1030158-conquering-heroes?p=1030235#post1030235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, does not you get in Contested Rolls the Exceptional Success only if you got 5 or <b>more</b> over your opponent. I.e. if my oponent roll 2 success, I need 7 success myself to get Exceptional Success?</div> </div> </div> </div>The rules don't describe that anywhere. Exceptional Successes occur on 5 or more successes. There's no exception for contested actions. If I get 10 successes and you get 8, the only reason you don't get an exceptional too is because you can't both fail (because you got less than me) and succeed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> NWoD Core p. 130:<br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">Note that in a contested action, the total successes <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">rolled for each participant are compared, and he with the <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">higher total wins. The difference between successes rolled <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">is not the \u201cmargin of success.\u201d So, if one participant gets <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">two successes and the other gets five, the latter of the two <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">wins with five successes. He doesn\u2019t win with three, the <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">difference between the two totals.&quot;</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>I see no indication this has changed in 2E<br /> <br /> Edit: This is reiterated in CofD page 69:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When two people fight over a specific goal, they engage in a contested action. You roll your dice pool and the Storyteller (or other player) rolls the dice pool for the other party. Whoever rolls the most successes is the victor. <b>Note that you count the total number of successes rolled when working out if you scored an exceptional success \u2014 don\u2019t subtract the other party\u2019s successes from yours</b>. A contested action takes up the action of the person initiating the action; resisting it is a reflexive action. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 01-11-2017, 05:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T14:20:02-08:00","id":1030246,"title":"","content":"Hmm, <b>Inodiv</b>, almost 12 years of running Storytelling System and always finding new things I'm doing wrong. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T14:20:46-08:00","id":1030247,"title":"","content":"Dodging cancels successes on the attack roll one for one, so it's not like 2e has no precedent for that kind of system. It doesn't seem to be the norm however.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T14:21:23-08:00","id":1030249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1030158-conquering-heroes?p=1030241#post1030241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not making them all out to be horrible people has helped. But while the book offers a lot of interesting antagonists, Beast still doesn't seem appealing from a gaming point of view, for me, at least. I think it would be really big with the 'I don't like these covenants or tribes or orders and so forth' crowd. A more pared down 'play a monster' game.'</div> </div> </div> </div>True. The game is still strained, but the cancerous tumor removed while leaving the benign one is still a large step in the right direction. Truth is, I'm going to be refluffing a lot of these guys as hunters (the Lightseeker's pretty much wannabe Buffy already), but I'm pleased about where the game is facing.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Although the book does well in confirming that &quot;terrible people&quot; can be sympathetic too. Michael Bellinger, the philanthropic serial killer who finds that hurting &quot;good people&quot; just isn't fun. Honestly I see myself (when playing Grand Theft Auto) in the guy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 01-11-2017, 05:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T14:29:53-08:00","id":1030251,"title":"","content":"I think the introduction of Hives went a long way to relieving the &quot;not enough of a society&quot; issue for me. The only tweak i found necessary for a more compelling Beast society is allowing Beasts to feed on other Beasts, so a Hoarder Apex can extract taxation that some will fight against, a Nemesis Apex will police &quot;lesser&quot; Beasts with her own sense of justice, etc etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 01-11-2017, 07:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T14:40:02-08:00","id":1030257,"title":"","content":"I'm generally digging the Insatiable conceptually but their rules and mechanics are a hot mess. Not sure why they would need a Lair (or rate Lair 0) if they already cause this Schism thing... and mechanically rolling the Schism rating in places where Satiety is called for might make a tad more sense otherwise I'm hard pressed to see when exactly a Beast might actually consider an Insatiable an actual threat...I foresee a weekend of hacking in the future...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T14:40:24-08:00","id":1030258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1030158-conquering-heroes?p=1030221#post1030221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So can someone tell me just what the Insatiable are?</div> </div> </div> </div>Haven't read it in detail yet, but my impression is if you think of the Begotten in relation to the Temenos (the collective unconscious of humanity), the Insatiable are their counterparts corresponding to the Anima Mundi (the unconsciousness of the Earth itself).<br /> <br /> They appear to have a Stryx/Idigam/etc type relationship to the Begotten as the &quot;things that the monsters tell horror stories about&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T21:10:02-08:00","id":1030414,"title":"","content":"So what do the the Insatiable actually do to antagonize Beasts? I see some references in this thread to hijacking Lairs and something called Schism, but what does that actually translate to? What is their particular predatory motivation?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T21:12:53-08:00","id":1030416,"title":"","content":"So, speaking as a high school teacher who works closely with OTs... Matt, that was one of the best written intros I've read. You absolutely nailed. Not surprising, given your full-time job, but I feel like there were a lot of places that fiction could a been fouled by another writer. Instead, you totally got me into it and could have made me believe it was real.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T21:13:34-08:00","id":1030418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1030158-conquering-heroes?p=1030257#post1030257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm generally digging the Insatiable conceptually but their rules and mechanics are a hot mess. Not sure why they would need a Lair (or rate Lair 0) if they already cause this Schism thing... and mechanically rolling the Schism rating in places where Satiety is called for might make a tad more sense otherwise I'm hard pressed to see when exactly a Beast might actually consider an Insatiable an actual threat...I foresee a weekend of hacking in the future...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Schism doesn't strike me as something that would keep the Insatiable safe in their own pocket dimension, nor do I think they can call on it for Tilts. It just causes mortals to act crazy.<br /> <br /> And I fail to see where they don't get Satiety when they want it. They just eat people to do so.<br /> <br /> (Speaking of Insatiable: Can I say I love Null Snyper for how much of an unrepentant, petty bitch she is? She's just <i>so </i>much of the worst parts of the Internet rolled together and turned into a Japanese horror flick that I have such a fun time making plans about how she gets her comeuppance and makes the players miserable in the meantime. I wonder how her manchild goons will feel when they realize their &quot;friend&quot; is a woman who thinks of them like a bunch of sporks..).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T21:21:59-08:00","id":1030422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1030158-conquering-heroes?p=1030414#post1030414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what do the the Insatiable actually do to antagonize Beasts? I see some references in this thread to hijacking Lairs and something called Schism, but what does that actually translate to? What is their particular predatory motivation?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They're nearly sociopathic-something about the Moment (their Devouring) completely destroys any recognizable humanity in them; they need to kill to feed, and they don't care. Bad enough, except they're <i>always </i>hungry, they're just not starving at Satiety 10. They're what happens when Beasts simply don't give a single solitary shit about trying to turn their Hungers into something productive, dialed up to 11.<br /> <br /> Beyond the purely moral reason, Insatiable can &quot;raid&quot; Lairs by entering them, gradually transforming the environment into something that suits and feeds them. The Primordial Dream hates this and starts turning it back to normal if the invader is forced out, but until then it belongs and gives power to the Obscene One. Worse, they can use their Horrors to <i>possess </i>Begotten, especially if they're at higher Satiety levels. The Schism is another reason-the longer an Insatiable stays in the area, the more she assaults the Primordial Dream by dint of her existence, causing primal fears from before humanity evolved to enter into the minds of mortals nearby. To put it simply, everyone becomes a paranoid, delusional nutcase who panics and attacks at the slightest provocation, if the Lamashtu stays there long enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T21:27:20-08:00","id":1030423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1030158-conquering-heroes?p=1030258#post1030258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Haven't read it in detail yet, but my impression is if you think of the Begotten in relation to the Temenos (the collective unconscious of humanity), the Insatiable are their counterparts corresponding to the Anima Mundi (the unconsciousness of the Earth itself).<br /> <br /> They appear to have a Stryx/Idigam/etc type relationship to the Begotten as the &quot;things that the monsters tell horror stories about&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>So: in a game founded on the subversion of the traditional hero-vs-beast dynamic, we're getting beast-like monsters that are so horrific that Beast-vs-Insatiable resembles the traditional hero-vs-beast dynamic? Interesting\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T21:31:42-08:00","id":1030425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1030158-conquering-heroes?p=1030414#post1030414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what do the the Insatiable actually do to antagonize Beasts? I see some references in this thread to hijacking Lairs and something called Schism, but what does that actually translate to? What is their particular predatory motivation?</div> </div> </div> </div>They'll steal Lairs, primarily, and Atavisms. They look down on Beasts, which given their attitude is probably antagonistic enough. It hops around a little, but they're rejected members of the 'family,' who want what they believe they deserve. The Astral Realm thing was really embraced, as they are not standard human fears but of the world's memories.<br /> <br /> The Schism is sort of like Disquiet, a roiling paranoia among people in the area. It's has a negative impact on the Primordial Dream but mechanically it just offers a potentially substantial, 1 to 10, penalty to social rolls in the area. Supposedly the Insatiate can guide the Schism but they suffer the penalty as well.<br /> <br /> They'll probably make good antagonists in other games. They'd definitely be on the werewolf hit list, considering Schism wrecks the Gauntlet pretty good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-12-2017, 12:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T21:35:20-08:00","id":1030427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1030158-conquering-heroes?p=1030423#post1030423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So: in a game founded on the subversion of the traditional hero-vs-beast dynamic, we're getting beast-like monsters that are so horrific that Beast-vs-Insatiable resembles the traditional hero-vs-beast dynamic? Interesting\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think it can work if they're not overused. Especially in response to players starting to take their characters' own predations too lightly. But certainly that conflict should not be a norm the game should focus on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T21:40:56-08:00","id":1030429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1030158-conquering-heroes?p=1030418#post1030418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The Schism doesn't strike me as something that would keep the Insatiable safe in their own pocket dimension, nor do I think they can call on it for Tilts. It just causes mortals to act crazy.<br /> <br /> And I fail to see where they don't get Satiety when they want it. They just eat people to do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>So let me get this straight. They burn 3 Satiety to get into one of the Lair's Chambers and then enter into a contested roll based on their Satiety. You expect me to believe that it just brought a human along to re-up it's dice pool like some kind of happy meal on legs?<br /> <br /> Sorry, I'm not buying it. The mechanics are a mess. Like the first draft of Heroes, I'm not convinced that Insatiable pose anything more than a mild annoyance to Beasts. But YMMV and like everything else, it's quite fixable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T21:50:55-08:00","id":1030434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1030158-conquering-heroes?p=1030429#post1030429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So let me get this straight. They burn 3 Satiety to get into one of the Lair's Chambers and then enter into a contested roll based on their Satiety. You expect me to believe that it just brought a human along to re-up it's dice pool like some kind of happy meal on legs?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is weird. The roll is against the Beast's Willpower + Lair, too. Their powers seem interesting in description but the mechanics for them sort of fall flat. The Schism being a social penalty is pretty weak, and the Insatiate suffering from it too seems to go against their description.<br /> <br /> EDIT: It might be referring to the Obedience Esurient, but it's more of an obey, not insinuate.<br /> <br /> The Player's Guide seriously needs to add some sort of Beast Akashic Record, too. Everyone seems expected to know about things without having anyone who would tell them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-12-2017, 01:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T21:57:44-08:00","id":1030436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1030158-conquering-heroes?p=1030429#post1030429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So let me get this straight. They burn 3 Satiety to get into one of the Lair's Chambers and then enter into a contested roll based on their Satiety. You expect me to believe that it just brought a human along to re-up it's dice pool like some kind of happy meal on legs?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because as we all know, a monster that specifically wreaks havoc through the Primordial Dream and gains benefits analogous to a physical merger with a Horror (which include increased Attributes) would never use a less costly route into a Beast's Lair that goes through the hive, and certainly couldn't have more than above-average Presence like <i>two thirds of the example characters </i>do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T23:53:59-08:00","id":1030457,"title":"","content":"Actually, there is one precedent for contested action subtracting successes from the other roll: Containing Paradox in Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T00:26:33-08:00","id":1030461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1030158-conquering-heroes?p=1030457#post1030457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, there is one precedent for contested action subtracting successes from the other roll: Containing Paradox in Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's not really a contested roll, more like a dodge one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T02:01:43-08:00","id":1030479,"title":"","content":"Have only read the introductory chapter. The blurbs on Heroes and particularly monstrous Beasts are about what I expected for a Night Horrors book.<br /> <br /> The Insatiables my first thought being:<br /> <br /> &quot;...so they're just Idigam for Beasts?&quot;<br /> <br /> Complete with the whole being an ancient race of creatures older then Beasts, being apart of an unknowable section of the Begotten's home turf, their primary deity casting them out but not able to definitively kill them, and now them being back to make the Begotten as miserable as possible. Haven't heard that one before...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T03:29:53-08:00","id":1030500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1030158-conquering-heroes?p=1030479#post1030479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have only read the introductory chapter. The blurbs on Heroes and particularly monstrous Beasts are about what I expected for a Night Horrors book.<br /> <br /> The Insatiables my first thought being:<br /> <br /> &quot;...so they're just Idigam for Beasts?&quot;<br /> <br /> Complete with the whole being an ancient race of creatures older then Beasts, being apart of an unknowable section of the Begotten's home turf, their primary deity casting them out but not able to definitively kill them, and now them being back to make the Begotten as miserable as possible. Haven't heard that one before...</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolf doesn't has a ownership to the idea of mad ancient beings. It was a idea created by lovecraft","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T04:29:00-08:00","id":1030518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1030158-conquering-heroes?p=1030479#post1030479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have only read the introductory chapter. The blurbs on Heroes and particularly monstrous Beasts are about what I expected for a Night Horrors book.<br /> <br /> The Insatiables my first thought being:<br /> <br /> &quot;...so they're just Idigam for Beasts?&quot;<br /> <br /> Complete with the whole being an ancient race of creatures older then Beasts, being apart of an unknowable section of the Begotten's home turf, their primary deity casting them out but not able to definitively kill them, and now them being back to make the Begotten as miserable as possible. Haven't heard that one before...</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like they are the Primordial Dreams understanding of all the &quot;Nemesis&quot; or &quot;Ancient Horror&quot; creatures... which works since we as humans have a Fasination about them...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T06:12:47-08:00","id":1030539,"title":"","content":"Potential buyer wondering, 'bestiary' sourcebooks about non-playable antagonists and RPG material about 'Van Helsing' mortal hunters of supernaturals typically rate very low in my interest and priority scale. I usually get moved to buy the former only late in a game's development cycle for sheer completist purposes, if I can find a good bargain sale, or if I heard the book somehow has stuff with significant potential use for character development. I almost never bother to buy 'hunter' games - definitely including any WoD/CoD version of Hunter, with the single exception of Dark Ages: Inquisitor - since I find the concept extremely boring and unappealing (even more so than Promethean, and that's a lot). Given these preferences of mine, how much do you think Conquering Heroes might potentially turn interesting and useful for me, if any ? I am wondering if it would be worthwhile and not too much of a disappointment for me, given my high general interest in the game line, for me to buy the book now or I should better wait at least until Beast Player's Guide is released.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 01-12-2017, 11:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T07:50:31-08:00","id":1030584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1030158-conquering-heroes?p=1030539#post1030539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given these preferences of mine, how much do you think Conquering Heroes might potentially turn interesting and useful for me, if any ? I am wondering if it would be worthwhile and not too much of a disappointment for me, given my high general interest in the game line, for me to buy the book now or I should better wait at least until Beast Player's Guide is released.</div> </div> </div> </div>While it is pretty cheap, the book seems to have just things you wouldn't be interested in. The first chapter is heroes, the second is Beasts, usually of the 'run amok' sort but at the least not ones most players would enjoy playing, and the third are Insatiates, which it suggests shouldn't be played. You could have a player be an Insatiate but, by the book at least, they don't work well with other Beasts.<br /> <br /> I'm big on playable antagonists as well. I'm sure the Insatiate could be done pretty easily with other monsters, but they wouldn't work well within the confines of a Beast game. Their Schism radiation acts sort of like Disquiet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-12-2017, 11:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T10:38:06-08:00","id":1030658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1030158-conquering-heroes?p=1030584#post1030584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While it is pretty cheap, the book seems to have just things you wouldn't be interested in. The first chapter is heroes, the second is Beasts, usually of the 'run amok' sort but at the least not ones most players would enjoy playing, and the third are Insatiates, which it suggests shouldn't be played. You could have a player be an Insatiate but, by the book at least, they don't work well with other Beasts.<br /> <br /> I'm big on playable antagonists as well. I'm sure the Insatiate could be done pretty easily with other monsters, but they wouldn't work well within the confines of a Beast game. Their Schism radiation acts sort of like Disquiet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the advice, but what a pity. The blurb misled me to think the book had worthwhile info on Inheritance Beasts instead of the Insatiates, and that had piqued my interest. While the other Inheritance types do make a character pretty much unplayable and useless except as the 'animalistic' kind of antagonist draugr and lesser spirits represent, I entirely regard Incarnate Beasts as very useful and fitting as 'elder' NPC and PC options in high-power, high-stakes games, the same as vampire elders and archmages. So I'm eager for additional stuff on them.<br /> <br /> From what you and others have said, I'm getting a vibe of the Insatiates being rather like the Strix for vampires, the Banishers for mages, or the Pandorans for Prometheans: e.g. the 'odd' supernaturals that hunt and harass the 'normal' type of their own splat for their own reasons and are bogeymen for the bogeymen, being effective enough to be a serious threat, but not so powerful as to owerwhelm their targets on a regular basis (unlike say the Gentry for changelings, or the God-Machine for demons).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 01-12-2017, 01:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T10:42:42-08:00","id":1030663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1030158-conquering-heroes?p=1030658#post1030658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks for the advice, but what a pity. The blurb misled me to think the book had worthwhile info on Inheritance Beasts instead of the Insatiates, and that had piqued my interest. While the other Inheritance types do make a character pretty much unplayable and useless except as the 'animalistic' kind of antagonist draugr and lesser spirits represent, I entirely regard Incarnate Beasts as very useful and fitting as 'elder' NPC and PC options in high-power, high-stakes games, the same as vampire elders and archmages. So I'm eager for additional stuff on them.<br /> <br /> From what you and others have said, I'm getting a vibe of the Insatiates being rather like the Strix for vampires, the Banishers for mages, or the Pandorans for Prometheans: e.g. the 'odd' supernaturals that hunt and harass the 'normal' type of their own splat for their own reasons and are bogeymen for the bogeymen, being effective enough to be a serious threat, but not so powerful as to owerwhelm their targets on a regular basis (unlike say the Gentry for changelings, or the God-Machine for demons).</div> </div> </div> </div>To be clear most (all?) of the sample Beasts are ones who have achieved one of the Inheritances, and you can gain some fluff insight into how to play them from it, but there's no mechanics, or anything that makes them more playable than they are in Beast Core.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T10:44:58-08:00","id":1030665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1030158-conquering-heroes?p=1030663#post1030663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be clear most (all?) of the sample Beasts are ones who have achieved one of the Inheritances, and you can gain some fluff insight into how to play them from it, but there's no mechanics, or anything that makes them more playable than they are in Beast Core.</div> </div> </div> </div>All but one.<br /> <br /> You're actually in luck though, two are Incarnates; one's a somewhat mercenary potential ally, the other is BBEG material.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T10:45:04-08:00","id":1030666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1030158-conquering-heroes?p=1030658#post1030658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the advice, but what a pity. The blurb had mislead me to think the book had worthwhile info on Inheritance Beasts instead of the Insatiates, and that had piqued my interest. While the other Inheritance types make a character pretty much unplayable and useless except as the 'mindless' kind of antagonist draugr and spirits represent, I entirely regard Incarnate Beasts as very useful and fitting as recurring NPCs and PC options in high-power, high-stakes games, the same as vampire elders and archmages. So I'm eager for additional stuff on them.</div> </div> </div> </div>It has Inheritance Beasts in the Beasts section. Two Incarnate, two Rampant, two Unfettered. The Slimy Lobbyist is the only standard Beast, and he's made repugnant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> From what you and others have said, I'm getting a vibe of the Insatiates being rather like the Strix for vampires, the Banishers for mages, or the Pandorans for Prometheans: e.g. the 'odd' supernaturals that hunt and harass the 'normal' type of their own splat for their own reasons and are bogeymen for the bogeymen, being effective enough to be a serious threat, but not so powerful as to owerwhelm their targets on a regular basis (unlike say the Gentry for changelings, or the God-Machine for demons). </div> </div> </div>I view them as more like the Deceived. They're clearly more related to Beasts than the strix are to vampires. Their motives are more like the strix, though. They don't need to eat Beasts the way Pandorans need energy from Prometheans. They just like to because they don't like them them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-12-2017, 01:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T10:57:53-08:00","id":1030673,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of Insatiable because I feel that Heroes weren't really effective antagonists. They can of course cause all kinds of problems, but they don't really have an air of dread about them. I guess what I'm saying is that Beasts know too much about them and what they can do.<br /> <br /> I found Null Snyper to be a bit too heavy handed though. The idea that a certain controversy about ethics in games journalism was caused by a primordial monstrosity is pretty comical. The thought of being attacked through webcams and the like is a great idea though. I definitely like the idea of her &quot;stretching her wings&quot; and eventually becoming a terror to rival the likes of The Blind Man.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5391-krycanelo","name":"Krycanelo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5391_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T11:18:43-08:00","id":1030681,"title":"","content":"Not quite sure I'm understanding how Insatiates &quot;steal&quot; Lairs, considering a Beast can't really live without one. I can see the subverting aspect, but the Lair is still the Beasts... <br /> <br /> I'm tempted to build upon it, where an Insatiate corrupts and claims Chamber after Chamber of a Beast's Lair until they're only left with their Heart Chamber. Killing the weakened Beast then keeps the Lair existing (minus the Heart Chamber), giving the Insatiate a Lair of their own. But only for a period of time before the Chambers degrade and collapse on themselves, leaving them to hunt another Beast for a new home. <br /> <br /> Maybe I need to reread it again, I'm just not quite grasping what they do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T11:21:09-08:00","id":1030682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krycanelo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1030158-conquering-heroes?p=1030673#post1030673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea of Insatiable because I feel that Heroes weren't really effective antagonists. They can of course cause all kinds of problems, but they don't really have an air of dread about them. I guess what I'm saying is that Beasts know too much about them and what they can do.<br /> <br /> I found Null Snyper to be a bit too heavy handed though. The idea that a certain controversy about ethics in games journalism was caused by a primordial monstrosity is pretty comical. The thought of being attacked through webcams and the like is a great idea though. I definitely like the idea of her &amp;quot;stretching her wings&amp;quot; and eventually becoming a terror to rival the likes of The Blind Man.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never got that. I got the sense she found a bunch of malcontents she knew, being a vicious troll already, and simply nudged what was already there.<br /> <br /> Thing is, I think that's probably why I don't have a problem. Hang around feminist support websites for a while, and one gets the sense that online misogynists and pick-up artists being manipulated by a fairy tale hag who eats suicides would result in a moral improvement. They are not nice people, and if you happen to feed on misery, such folk are just a pragmatic option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T11:24:05-08:00","id":1030686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krycanelo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1030158-conquering-heroes?p=1030673#post1030673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I found Null Snyper to be a bit too heavy handed though. The idea that a certain controversy about ethics in games journalism was caused by a primordial monstrosity is pretty comical.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think the implication is that she <i>caused </i>totallyaboutethicsingamesjournalismgate, it's just that she uses its supporters to her ends, which by all accounts is real easy to do if you're a worse enough person...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T11:29:45-08:00","id":1030692,"title":"","content":"By the way, this book has immensely helped me in liking the released Beast's version of Heroes over the preview version. The only thing I'd change is have a category called Dream-Touched (or whatever), with Heroes being a subclass of that category who are specifically antagonistic to Beasts. But honestly, that's a very minor gripe and very semantic. <br /> <br /> Still, it's given me a thought of a NPC who touches the shallows of the Primordial Dream but seeks to understand. Maybe a psychologist with a study of the meaning of dreams that's willing to converse with Beasts. I just can't really think of that kind of a character as a &quot;Hero&quot; though. More like a &quot;Shaman&quot; or &quot;Questor&quot; or &quot;Seeker&quot;, I guess. Like I said, very semantic in basis, but I generally view that semantics is important.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T11:35:08-08:00","id":1030697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1030158-conquering-heroes?p=1030686#post1030686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think the implication is that she <i>caused </i>totallyaboutethicsingamesjournalismgate, it's just that she uses its supporters to her ends, which by all accounts is real easy to do if you're a worse enough person...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I interpreted it as her taking advantage of it and feeding those people targets, instead of being an originator. A big theme of the Insatiates is that they don't really MAKE anything, they just subvert and turn to their own purposes to fulfill their Hunger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T11:56:49-08:00","id":1030703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1030158-conquering-heroes?p=1030697#post1030697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I interpreted it as her taking advantage of it and feeding those people targets, instead of being an originator. A big theme of the Insatiates is that they don't really MAKE anything, they just subvert and turn to their own purposes to fulfill their Hunger.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> &quot; she whipped up an angry mob to go after her targets. Through empty rhetoric and carefully coordinated campaigns of doxing and harassment, she terrorized players, game developers, and journalists in the industry who don\u2019t share her trolls\u2019 views.&quot;<br /> <br /> I interpreted it as that these man children existed on the internet before but were relatively benign and uncoordinated, but she was the one who masterminded GG since it says she did it, not her trolls. My problem is that it goes against the Insatiable's theme of subversion. It's not that she subverted and corrupted a legitimate campaign about ethics in games journalism, it's that her trolls, under her control, created it. Then again, this could all feed into the idea that Snyper is on the cusp of becoming something different, an evolved form of an insatiable born from the internet transcending humanity to the point where it is equal to a force of nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5391-krycanelo","name":"Krycanelo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5391_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T12:27:31-08:00","id":1030724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krycanelo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1030158-conquering-heroes?p=1030703#post1030703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> &amp;quot; she whipped up an angry mob to go after her targets. Through empty rhetoric and carefully coordinated campaigns of doxing and harassment, she terrorized players, game developers, and journalists in the industry who don\u2019t share her trolls\u2019 views.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> I interpreted it as that these man children existed on the internet before but were relatively benign and uncoordinated, but she was the one who masterminded GG since it says she did it, not her trolls. My problem is that it goes against the Insatiable's theme of subversion. It's not that she subverted and corrupted a legitimate campaign about ethics in games journalism, it's that her trolls, under her control, created it. Then again, this could all feed into the idea that Snyper is on the cusp of becoming something different, an evolved form of an insatiable born from the internet transcending humanity to the point where it is equal to a force of nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>I came away with a different interpretation. <br /> <br /> &quot;Recently, Null Snyper discovered the adolescent man-children that exist where gamers and men's rights activists overlap. She felt nothing but contempt for them, but she decided to try flexing her Internet muscles. Instead of driving people to suicide through direct online interaction, she whipped up an angry mob to go after her targets. Through empty rhetoric and carefully coordinated campaigns of doxing and harassment, she terrorized players, game developers, and journalists in the industry who don't share her trolls' views.&quot;<br /> <br /> There's no specific mention of GG. Only reference to common circles. It points out that these people already existed, and all she did was fan the flames and provide coordination to very specific campaigns against particular people. So this suggests to me that she's subverting an already existing group to direct them against targets of her choosing. <br /> <br /> There is no mention of a legitimate campaign or the creation of a movement, whether legitimate or illegitimate. The &quot;coordinated campaigns&quot; is specifically in reference to efforts to dox and harass particular victims. <br /> <br /> That's why I come away interpreting there being a movement similar to GG that Null Snyper noticed and took advantage of to cause trouble. So I don't think she's particularly responsible for it, though she's used it to her own advantage. I like that interpretation, because humans can be pretty awful on our own and I don't think we need to have an actual monster be involved to explain how something like GG happened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T13:27:28-08:00","id":1030750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1030158-conquering-heroes?p=1030416#post1030416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, speaking as a high school teacher who works closely with OTs... Matt, that was one of the best written intros I've read. You absolutely nailed. Not surprising, given your full-time job, but I feel like there were a lot of places that fiction could a been fouled by another writer. Instead, you totally got me into it and could have made me believe it was real.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! Parts of the story really did happen (not the &quot;smashing someone's head in with a geode&quot; part, obviously).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T14:46:51-08:00","id":1030809,"title":"","content":"Wow, coming right out and bluntly shitting on MRAs and Gamergaters, damn is there a reason you so desperate to pick a fight with Gamergaters and MRAs Matt? <br /> <br /> As an MRA I'm curious as to why you have a hate on for us Matt? <br /> <br /> So whose Null Synder supposed to be a proxi for? Mercedes Carrera? One of the Honeybadgers? Diana Davidson? <br /> <br /> I'm genuinely curious why you have such a low opinion of us and what I can do to convince you we aren't so bad that we need to be turned into villians? <br /> <br /> I think at this point I'll pass if this book is just a vechile for Matt's vendettas, I have better things to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T15:11:49-08:00","id":1030818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1030158-conquering-heroes?p=1030809#post1030809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow, coming right out and bluntly shitting on MRAs and Gamergaters, damn is there a reason you so desperate to pick a fight with Gamergaters and MRAs Matt?<br /> <br /> As an MRA I'm curious as to why you have a hate on for us Matt?<br /> <br /> So whose Null Synder supposed to be a proxi for? Mercedes Carrera? One of the Honeybadgers? Diana Davidson?<br /> <br /> I'm genuinely curious why you have such a low opinion of us and what I can do to convince you we aren't so bad that we need to be turned into villians?<br /> <br /> I think at this point I'll pass if this book is just a vechile for Matt's vendettas, I have better things to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Matt didn't develop the book. He wrote the introductory story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T15:22:59-08:00","id":1030822,"title":"","content":"Just finished the Insatiable chapter. So, so happy with them, both in concept and the examples presented. An extra class of antagonists is what I feel Beast needed, and they are close to some ideas I had, only more refined and fully described. Now to unleash them on my players <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T15:28:02-08:00","id":1030826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1030158-conquering-heroes?p=1030818#post1030818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Matt didn't develop the book. He wrote the introductory story.</div> </div> </div> </div> Apology withdrawn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 01-12-2017, 07:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T16:00:25-08:00","id":1030840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1030158-conquering-heroes?p=1030826#post1030826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then I apologize to Matt utterly, I was going on what was revealed in this thread. If he wasn't the source I apologize.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still, you're going too hard, null mysteris could be anyone that uses Internet to do evil things or hurt people?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T16:11:41-08:00","id":1030847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1030158-conquering-heroes?p=1030809#post1030809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow, coming right out and bluntly shitting on MRAs and Gamergaters, damn is there a reason you so desperate to pick a fight with Gamergaters and MRAs?<br /> <br /> As an MRA I'm curious as to why you have a hate on for us?<br /> <br /> I'm genuinely curious why you have such a low opinion of us and what I can do to convince you we aren't so bad that we need to be turned into villians?</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://m.popkey.co/49e5b4/EpbLm_s-200x150.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">thisdancegoesroundandroundandround</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T16:21:24-08:00","id":1030851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1030158-conquering-heroes?p=1030840#post1030840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still, you're going too hard, null 