 </div> <div class=\"message\">Guildhalls of the Deathless. There's an Utterance in the Su-Menent's chunk of Chapter Seven.<br /> <br /> &quot;Shepherds write that sometimes, a tall, cruel-looking man dressed as ancient royalty stands amidst the crawling chaos, half in shadow, and utters enigmatic statements somehow connected to the nearby witnesses.&quot;<br /> <br /> Lore of the Deceived, the supplement <i>to</i> the supplement that was Book of the Deceived. He shows up in an Utterance that hard-bans most immortal entities from material existence for a millennium.<br /> <br /> &quot;What such cosmic entities may do in revenge for such banishment even without a physical body is another matter altogether. Legends among the Deceived speak of the Ochre-Masked King, a primordial demon who has plagued the world's preeminent civilizations once every thousand years until he can be sent back bodiless once more to the hellscape from whence he came.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Words of Dead Fury also summons a Chthonic Being, which really gives every impression of being a Shoggoth or something.<br /> <br /> Mummy is full to the brim with Lovecraft.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T00:00:15-08:00","id":1031031,"title":"","content":"...I know it's a poor defense, but I purposefully didn't read all of the Utterances to keep some suprise just in case I ever got to be a player character. <br /> <br /> That being said, yaaaaaaa I should have first thought of Mummy: the Curse when thinking about Lovecraft analogues in the CofD. - . -'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","da